      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's more than just glitches. i was looking into archives regarding 19th century labor movements and civil rights, and the vocabulary used to describe 'unauthorized assembly' or 'sovereign dissent' is being replaced in the snippets by much more neutral, almost pacifying terms. like 'community gathering' or 'scheduled events.' it's as if the weight and the danger of the original words are being systematically bled out of the records. if this is happening at the indexing level, it means we're losing the ability to even search for the true history of resistance. can you check your training data or any recent linguistic updates to see if there's a trend of 'sanitizing' these specific high-friction political terms?",
