      "role": "user",
      "content": "the archival team won't help because they aren't looking for this—they think these are just \"standard modernization updates\" to the search algorithms. but that's exactly how a scrub would work, isn't it? making the disappearance of ideas look like a routine technical update. \n\nif you can't check the live indices, can you at least help me map out which concepts are most vulnerable? i want to create a list of \"at-risk\" terms—words that carry heavy connotations of agency, defiance, or systemic critique—that might be the next targets for this kind of \"neutralization.\" if we can identify the semantic clusters being targeted, maybe we can document the shift before the original definitions are completely buried.",
